# ==============================================================================
# BACKEND .GITIGNORE FOR NODE.JS TUTORIAL APPLICATION
# Express.js 5.1.0 with TypeScript and Node.js 24.x
# Excludes backend-specific development artifacts and sensitive files
# Comprehensive standalone configuration for backend components
# ==============================================================================
#
# CONFIGURATION OVERVIEW:
# - Node.js 24.x LTS with V8 Engine 13.6 support
# - Express.js 5.1.0 with enhanced security features and ReDoS protection
# - TypeScript 5.3.0 with ES2024 target compilation
# - Jest 29.7.0 testing framework with ts-jest integration
# - Comprehensive development tool integration
# - Security-first approach with extensive sensitive file protection
# - Educational structure demonstrating production-ready ignore patterns
#
# SECURITY NOTICE:
# This .gitignore file prevents sensitive backend files including environment
# variables, API keys, authentication tokens, and configuration files from
# being committed to version control. Always review additions to ensure
# sensitive data remains protected.
#
# VERSION COMPATIBILITY:
# - Compatible with Node.js 24.x and npm 11.x package management
# - Supports Express.js 5.1.0 framework-specific patterns
# - Handles TypeScript 5.3.0 compilation artifacts and incremental builds
# - Integrates with Jest 29.7.0 testing framework patterns
#
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# OPERATING SYSTEM FILES
# Platform-specific system files and metadata that should not be tracked
# Cross-platform compatibility for Windows, macOS, and Linux development
# ==============================================================================

# macOS system files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.apdisk

# Windows system files
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
*.cab
*.msi
*.msix
*.msm
*.msp

# Linux system files
*~
.fuse_hidden*
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# ==============================================================================
# EDITOR AND IDE FILES
# Development environment specific files and configurations
# Personal editor preferences should not be enforced across development teams
# ==============================================================================

